ines, the address and Standard are still displayed, and \\\"Place order\\\" is enabled\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The orders API shall leave the stock quantity in the parts database unchanged when an order is placed or cancelled.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Part BP-200 with stock 10 when B1 places an order for 2 of BP-200 and then cancels it through the API then The parts row for BP-200 still has stock value 10 after each call\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The orders API shall return to a buyer only the orders placed by that buyer.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Buyer B1 has 2 orders and buyer B2 has 3 orders when B1 calls GET /api/orders then The returned list has exactly B1's 2 orders\",\n    \"Given Order ORD-000005 belongs to B2 when B1 calls GET /api/orders/ORD-000005 and POST /api/orders/ORD-000005/cancel then Each response status is 404 and the order row status is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a buyer requests their orders, the orders API shall return them newest first, each with order number, date placed, number of items (total of all quantities), total and status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given B1 placed ORD-000001 on 1 Oct (2 filters + 1 pad) and ORD-000002 on 3 Oct when B1 calls GET /api/orders then The returned list is ORD-000002 then ORD-000001, and ORD-000001 has fields datePlaced, itemCount 3, total and status\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the buyer picks a status filter on My orders, the orders API shall return only that buyer's orders with that status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given B1 has orders with statuses Placed, Placed and Cancelled when B1 calls GET /api/orders?status=Cancelled then The returned list has only the 1 Cancelled order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a buyer opens one of their orders, the orders API shall return its lines (part number, name, quantity, unit price), delivery address, delivery option, total and status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given B1's order ORD-000001 with 2 of BP-200 at £12.50, Next day, address \\\"1 High St, Leeds\\\" when B1 calls GET /api/orders/ORD-000001 then The response status is 200 and the response has the line {BP-200, Brake Pad, 2, 12.50}, address \\\"1 High St, Leeds\\\", deliveryOption NEXT_DAY, total 34.99 and status Placed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the buyer opens an order, the portal shall show a status timeline Placed → Packed → Dispatched → Delivered with the current status marked by text as well as colour.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order whose status was set to Dispatched in the database when the buyer opens it on My orders then The timeline shown lists the four steps in order, and Dispatched is marked as current with a text label, not by colour alone\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While an order's status is Placed, the portal shall show a \\\"Cancel order\\\" button in the order detail that asks for confirmation before calling the cancel API.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order with status Placed and one with status Packed when the buyer opens each one then \\\"Cancel order\\\" is shown only for the Placed order\",\n    \"Given The buyer pressed \\\"Cancel order\\\" on a Placed order when they decline the confirmation, then press it again and confirm then No cancel request is sent after declining; after confirming, the status shown becomes Cancelled and the button is no longer displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a buyer cancels their order whose status is still Placed, the orders API shall set the status to Cancelled.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given B1's order ORD-000001 with status Placed when B1 calls POST /api/orders/ORD-000001/cancel then The response status is 200, the response status field is \\\"Cancelled\\\", and the orders row has status Cancelled\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the order's status is no longer Placed when the buyer confirms cancelling, then the orders API shall refuse with status 409 and leave the status unchanged.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given B1's order ORD-000001 whose status was changed to Packed in the database when B1 calls POST /api/orders/ORD-000001/cancel then The response status is 409 with an error message, and the orders row status is still Packed\",\n    \"Given The buyer has an order open showing Placed, and its status was changed to Packed in the database when they press \\\"Cancel order\\\" and confirm then A message is shown saying the order can no longer be cancelled, the panel refreshes to show Packed, and \\\"Cancel order\\\" is no longer displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While the buyer has no orders, the portal shall show \\\"No orders yet\\\" and a link to Find parts on My orders.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Buyer B3 with no orders when B3 calls GET /api/orders then The response status is 200 and the returned list is empty\",\n    \"Given Buyer B3 with no orders when they open /orders then \\\"No orders yet\\\" and a link to /parts are shown\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall show all three screens without horizontal scrolling at viewport widths from 360 px upwards.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox when each screen is opened at 360 px, 768 px and 1280 px widths then No horizontal scroll bar is shown and every button and field is displayed and usable\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall give every form field a visible text label and let the buyer reach and use every control by keyboard alone.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The three screens with a cart containing 2 lines when a tester uses only the keyboard to search, filter, add to cart, change quantity, remove, place an order, open an order and cancel it then Every step can be completed, focus is always visible, and every field has a label announced by a screen reader\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While the parts database holds 5,000 parts, the Find parts screen shall load its first page of results in under 2 seconds.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given 5,000 parts seeded in the parts database when GET /api/parts?page=1&q=filter&category=Filters is called 100 times then The 95th-percentile response time is under 500 ms and each response status is 200\",\n    \"Given 5,000 parts seeded and a cold browser cache on a desktop with a 10 Mbps connection when a tester opens /parts then The first 20 parts are displayed within 2 seconds of navigation start\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the orders API rejects an order with a 409 stock conflict, the cart shall lower each affected line to the stock now available with the message \\\"Only n available\\\", remove each affected line whose available stock is 0 with the message \\\"<part name> is now out of stock\\\", and keep all other lines.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A CartStore holding 5 of BP-200, 1 of OF-100 \\\"Oil Filter\\\" and 2 of AF-300 when CartStore.applyStockLimits([{BP-200, 3}, {OF-100, 0}]) is called with the 409 response then The returned lines list has BP-200 with quantity value 3 and message \\\"Only 3 available\\\", AF-300 with quantity value 2, and no OF-100 line; the returned messages include \\\"Oil Filter is now out of stock\\\"\",\n    \"Given The CartStore after AC-39.1 when CartStore.lines() is called then Every returned line has a quantity value from 1 to 99 and CartStore.count() returns 5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While a place-order request is in progress, the checkout shall disable \\\"Place order\\\".\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A CheckoutForm with a 20-character address and delivery option Standard when CheckoutForm.startSubmit() is called and then CheckoutForm.canPlaceOrder() is called then The returned value is false\",\n    \"Given The CheckoutForm from AC-40.1 after startSubmit() when CheckoutForm.finishSubmit() is called and then CheckoutForm.canPlaceOrder() is called then The returned value is true\",\n    \"Given A buyer at checkout with a valid cart, address and delivery option, and the orders API delaying its response by 3 seconds when they press \\\"Place order\\\" twice within 1 second then The button is shown disabled until the response arrives and exactly one POST /api/orders request is sent\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the buyer opens the cart, the cart shall fetch the current price of each line's part from the parts API and use only those current prices for unit prices, line totals and totals.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A CartStore holding 3 of BP-200 saved at unit price 12.50, and a parts API client stub returning BP-200 with price 14.00 and stock 10 when CartStore.refresh(partsClient) is called and then CartStore.lines() and CartStore.subtotal() are called then One call is sent to the parts client for BP-200, the returned line has unitPrice 14.00 and lineTotal 42.00, and the returned subtotal value is 42.00\",\n    \"Given A buyer whose stored cart holds BP-200 saved at £12.50, while the parts database price for BP-200 is now £14.00 when they open /cart then The unit price shown is £14.00, the subtotal shown is based on £14.00, and £12.50 is not displayed anywhere on the page\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the current part data fetched when the cart opens shows a cart line's part has 0 stock, then the cart shall remove that line and give the message \\\"<part name> is now out of stock\\\".\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A CartStore holding 2 of OF-100 \\\"Oil Filter\\\" and 1 of BP-200, and a parts API client stub returning OF-100 with stock 0 and BP-200 with stock 10 when CartStore.refresh(partsClient) is called then The returned lines list contains only BP-200 with quantity value 1, the returned messages include \\\"Oil Filter is now out of stock\\\", and CartStore.count() returns 1\",\n    \"Given A CartStore whose only line is 1 of OF-100 \\\"Oil Filter\\\", and a parts API client 